omputer skills; can be grumpy; can be uncooperative.\n\nStrengths: stress resilience, conscientious (reliability), technical (weather, computer). Weaknesses: grumpy, uncooperative (crew cooperation).\n\nCandidate C: can anticipate dangerous situations; able to see complex connections; excellent spatial vision; very good leadership qualities; sometimes not good at taking criticism; can be unorganized.\n\nStrengths: anticipation, complex connections (technical competence), spatial vision, leadership. Weaknesses: not good at criticism (feedback), unorganized (reliability?).\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately; can concentrate very well; solves problems extremely well; takes responsibility seriously; regarded as arrogant; relatively weak leadership skills.\n\nStrengths: problem solving, concentration, responsibility. Weaknesses: arrogance, weak leadership.\n\nWe need to pick best overall fit. Likely Candidate C has strong technical and anticipation, leadership, but concerns about organization and feedback. Candidate B has stress resilience and technical, but uncooperative. Candidate A is reliable and crew positive but communication issues. Candidate D has responsibility and problem solving but arrogance and weak leadership.\n\nProbably Candidate C is strongest overall, despite feedback issues, but we need to discuss. Let's propose initial recommendation: Candidate C.\n\nWe need to reference facts: anticipation, complex connections, leadership, but note concerns: unorganized, not good at criticism.\n\nMake argument: overall fit best.\n\nProceed."}
